cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Who Prefers Structured Reasoning? AI Judges Do, Domain Experts Don't"
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the paper."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rubin
    given-names: Jordan
repository-code: "https://github.com/jordanrubin/who-prefers-structured-reasoning"
abstract: >-
  Code, configurations, epistemic-operation prompts, and aggregated evaluation
  scores for the paper "Who Prefers Structured Reasoning? AI Judges Do, Domain
  Experts Don't" — a study showing that a cognitively-scaffolded LLM corpus-
  synthesis pipeline produces large, cross-model LLM-as-judge gains that blinded
  domain experts do not perceive, exposing a structural failure mode in rubric-
  based synthesis evaluation.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - LLM-as-judge
  - evaluation
  - structured prompting
  - corpus synthesis
license: MIT
